#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1248 expect=skipped domain=EC
#note "FRESH: EC deliberately carries no ECDOSE column. ECOCCUR='N', so the applicability half is TRUE and only the absent value column can silence the rule. Predicted noViolation: Requirements.Variables.All [ECOCCUR] is satisfied (the column is present) so the rule EXECUTES, and the derived var_exists(\"ECDOSE\") conjunct is then false. Pins the difference between the two silencing channels -- an absent GATE variable reports a skip, an absent VALUE variable reports nothing at all. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset EC class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure as Collected"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ECSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ECTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col ECPRESP type=Char label="Pre-Specified"
col ECOCCUR type=Char label="Occurrence"
---
S1 | EC | 001 | 1 | DRUG A | Y | N
